WEBVTT

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:27.850
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:27.850
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:27.850
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.440 --> 00:02:01.850
The Mutineer
Chapter IV

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.600
Retract the anchors and prepare for free fall !

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.570
Retracted.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.920
Preparing for freefall.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.610
The destroyer, Hameln II, was undergoing
escape maneuvers under Reinhard orders...

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:29.080
...who had officially been designated by the captain to assume command of the ship.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.960
By free falling toward
the system's star Altmuel...

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.680
...and accelerating with the aid of the
starwind from the expected explosion...

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.130
...they intended to move past the enemy's encirclement.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.330
But it was a huge gamble.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.150
Is there any activity from the
approaching enemy ships ?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.750
They're behind the rocks so we can't know for sure, but we must be in their dead angle, too.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.330
Engine room, how
are the repairs going ?

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:57.260
They're going well so far.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:01.000
If you can, I'd like you to send
Seaman Schmitt up to the bridge.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.580
I want to have him
observe Altmuel, if possible.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:10.030
Since Rolf isn't here,
we're short handed.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.900
If you can send
down some backup...

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.330
Backup...

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.800
Shall I go ?

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.180
I'll go.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:22.300
No. 1 ?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.150
I have no place here.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:31.190
I'd like you to let me help
repair the engine at least.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:32.680
But...

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.010
I'm fully aware that the engine room will be a bed of needles for me.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.900
But to pay for what I did,
I want to work alongside them.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.630
I understand.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.570
I'll count on you.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.830
Are you sure this is okay ?

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:00.280
In the engine room, Zaidel
and the others can watch him.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.180
Maybe this works out better.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.780
And it's also a fact
that we're short handed.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:08.690
Chief Engineer, the First Officer is heading down there.

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.030
In exchange for him,
please send Schmitt up here.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.030
The First Officer ?

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.000
Roger.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.730
Any activities on the
surface of the star ?

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.090
They are as expected.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.750
Approximately five hours
till the explosion.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.360
How about the engine repairs ?

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.480
We need about four more hours.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.760
The margin is one hour...

00:04:55.870 --> 00:05:00.990
The interior temperature is presently 104 degrees Fahrenheit, and continues to rise.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.300
The cooling system has maxed out...

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.980
Unless the engine is operational, no power can be supplied to it.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:17.130
In one hour, we will move past the point
of no return from the star's gravity range.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.230
From that point forward...

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:20.680
...the ship will be unable to break away,
even with the engine at maximum output.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.100
We will continue with the operation.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.190
Sir...

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:30.860
I request permission
to leave the bridge.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.330
It may be because of the
heat, but I'm feeling ill.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.350
I need to go to sick bay.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:36.430
Very well.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.100
Lord Reinhard, LTJG Dewling
has boarded an escape pod.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.910
Right now, I am trying to
abort its ejection, but...

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:37.120
LTJG, LTJG Dewling,
what are you doing ?

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.070
I'm escaping.

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.600
I'll escape and ask the Alliance for help.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.070
That's insane.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.270
From the beginning, I
suggested that we surrender.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:48.790
I never wanted to go through
with a gamble like this.

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:51.220
I don't want to be burned alive.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.330
Don't interfere with me,
Ensign Kircheis !

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.390
This is worse than self-destruction !

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.280
We didn't need to
take this kind of risk !

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.130
All we had to do was surrender and become prisoners !

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.450
Lieutenant Junior Grade !

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.690
LTJG Musel is the
same as the First Officer.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.650
Their methods may differ,
but all they want is to be a hero !

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.690
I want no part of it.
I only want to live !

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.580
After the evacuation pod is released...

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.280
...there is a time lag before it can
send a rescue signal, right ?

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.680
About five seconds.

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:28.560
Chief Gunner, is it possible to destroy the pod with the anti-aircraft cannon within five seconds of release ?

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:31.730
Is it possible ?

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:34.590
It's possible, but...

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.020
Prepare to fire.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:41.470
Wait, Dewling has been
cooperative with you up to now.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:45.380
We cannot risk letting the enemy discover our ship's coordinates.

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.150
Prepare to fire.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.870
Anti-aircraft cannon, preparing to fire.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:53.590
Preparations completed.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.190
All right.

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:57.930
Ensign Kircheis, are you listening ?

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.930
Yes, Interim Captain.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.220
Release the pod.

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.150
We will shoot it
down from up here.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.130
Order acknowledged.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.280
What the hell am I going to do ?

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:21.950
What the hell am I going to do ?

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:27.090
I...I...what am I going to do ?

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:28.880
What am I...

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:32.740
It has been resolved.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:41.840
Cancel preparations to fire.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.510
Preparations canceled.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.850
You knew from the beginning
that this{i.e. Dewling changing his mind} would happen ?

00:08:49.930 --> 00:08:55.480
If we shot it down, its explosion might have led the enemy to discover our position.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:56.400
This was the best outcome.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:36.630
One hour until the
predicted explosion time.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:38.180
Any signs{of explosion} ?

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:40.830
You can't tell ?

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:43.250
I'm sorry...

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:46.170
This is the first time that I've
actually observed it at this range, so...

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.670
It's about time for the engine
repairs to be complete, right ?

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.390
Task completed.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:02.050
I'm done here, too.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:04.320
Okay.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.360
We'll test-start the engine.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.500
Prepare for the simulation
of the main engine ignition !

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.690
Preparation complete.

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:17.870
Ignite !

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:18.740
Ignite !

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:28.870
Ignition confirmed !

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:30.300
All right !

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:36.280
This is only a computer simulation
since we can't actually ignite it now...

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.480
...but it appears that the
repairs were successful.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.300
What ?

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:44.950
What happened ?

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.870
One of the positioning
thrusters isn't functioning !

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.580
It's Thruster #13.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:57.500
We were hit close to it, and we would
have liked to repair it from the outside...

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:02.150
...but I thought we could
do with an internal bypass.

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:06.050
No, actually when we tested it once, it did work as it was.

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.420
So the only solution is to
fix it from the outside.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:11.220
No way.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.710
It's impossible for us to
go outside at this point.

00:11:13.710 --> 00:11:16.540
The temperature is already past the
anti-heat limit of our space suits.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.630
It's just one thruster - 
can we do without it ?

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:21.590
We can't.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:26.260
When we get the starwind, it'll be necessary for us to turn our stern toward Altmuel.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.810
If we can't use #13...

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.520
How about if we roll the ship and move #13 inside the shadow ?

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:38.610
And if we use the solar panel to absorb heat and work underneath it we might be able to pull it off.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:39.870
Is it possible ?

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.320
Give me one second, please.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.430
If it's within ten minutes{we can}.

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:47.700
All right, I'll do it.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:49.750
I'm the one who proposed it.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.030
I'll do it.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:53.860
I can't trust you.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:55.470
One person can't do it.

00:11:55.470 --> 00:11:57.580
We need at least two people...

00:11:57.580 --> 00:12:00.900
...one absorbing the heat with the panel, and the other doing the repairs.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:03.930
Then, Bunto, you come with me.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:05.440
Huh ?

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:08.450
But...I'm not good at outboard work...

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.090
Now isn't the time
to be a coward !

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:11.350
Not that...

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:12.860
I don't feel confident.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.100
If I screw up, it's all over...

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:18.900
I'll do it.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.760
I want you to trust me,
just one more time.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.580
I understand.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:32.380
I'll count on you.

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.140
Petty Officer, are you okay with this ?

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.430
Can't be helped.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:46.650
We have less than 30 minutes till the
expected time for the surface explosion.

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:53.300
Outboard task, start.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:15.800
Task has been begun.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.200
Enemy ship detected !

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:26.080
Where is it ?

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.680
Outside of the third asteroid belt !

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.520
We've got the distance.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.290
But it seems they've
detected our movements.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.190
They're pursuing us !

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:39.920
They must have noticed the positioning thruster emissions from just now{from rolling the ship to move the #13 thruster into shadow}.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.940
But they probably won't
come inside the safety orbit.

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:56.970
The enemy ship has fired
several long range missiles !

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:04.030
Three minutes till missile impact !

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:10.110
Is it done yet ?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.690
Done !

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:16.920
Test !

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:21.110
Good !

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.180
You're out of time !

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:23.090
Hurry back !

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.480
30 seconds till missile impact !

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:40.740
It's coming !

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.710
It's the surface explosion !

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:49.830
Commence positioning !

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.080
Kircheis, have the crew
prepare for the shock{from the wind} !

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:23.810
Sir !

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:57.300
Outboard task completed.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.200
Petty Officer Zaidel has returned.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.900
Lieutenant Beltram has...

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:03.450
...died in the line of duty...

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:08.040
We're not finished !

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:09.640
The starwind is coming !

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.680
Positioning complete !

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.900
15 seconds till the impact of the starwind.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.430
All crew, prepare for shock !

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:21.150
Commence countdown !

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:22.680
Ten...{in German}

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.680
...nine...{in German}

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:24.680
...eight...{in German}

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.700
When the starwind hits, ignite the engine !

00:16:24.680 --> 00:16:25.680
...seven...{in German}

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:26.880
...six...{in German}

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:27.980
...five...{in German}

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:28.930
...four...{in German}

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:29.930
...three...{in German}

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:30.930
...two...{in German}

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:31.930
...one...{in German}

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.050
Ignite the engine !

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:34.880
Go !

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:59.210
This is destroyer Hameln II, under Imperial Force Destroyer Unit 237.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:02.430
We encountered an enemy
fleet in Starzone Altmuel.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.180
All friendly ships have been destroyed.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:05.280
We request reinforcements.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:10.610
This is destroyer Hameln II, Interim Captain, Lieutenant Junior Grade Reinhard von Musel.

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:17.230
This is cruiser Selarkrantz
{Note: inaudible} under the Merkatz Fleet.

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:19.300
Request acknowledged.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.540
One fleet unit has
already been dispatched.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:22.540
Please join them.

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:28.540
Hameln II acknowledges.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:29.730
We thank you for
the reinforcements.

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:31.300
We did it !

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:32.630
We're saved !

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:33.860
We're safe now !

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:34.520
We did it !

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:35.480
We did it !

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.430
We were saved...?

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.010
What a job he's done.

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:43.930
See ?

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:05.020
I told them not to put
more stress on the injured.

00:18:09.110 --> 00:18:10.680
Doctor...

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:11.770
...what's happening ?

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:15.090
Your judgment paid off.

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.530
That kid pulled it off, and we're saved.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.690
We'll soon be able to
join up with our allies.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.180
I see...

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:24.200
...what about the First Officer ?

00:18:25.990 --> 00:18:27.540
He's dead.

00:18:30.030 --> 00:18:34.500
He fixed the engine, saved his
subordinate, and sacrificed himself.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.000
I see...

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.400
He was an honorable officer, till the end.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.280
Yes, that's what it is...

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:51.280
The Alliance fleet that
had invaded Starzone Altmuel...

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:57.580
...fled without putting up a fight as soon as the
Imperial fleet arrived to aid the Hameln II.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:02.750
LTJG Reinhard von Musel received a promotion not only for his command of the ship...

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:07.680
...in the absence of the Captain and First Officer and their return as the unit's sole surviving vessel...

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:14.350
...but also for warning of the enemy's
encroachment, preventing their invasion.

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:20.840
I am honored to receive the promotion, but is it really all right ?

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.390
What are you talking about ?

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:27.030
Um, I thought I would be
held accountable for mutiny.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:30.750
There has been no occurrence
of mutiny on my ship.

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:39.490
I was lethargic, so the chronological order of events in my report may be a little off...

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:43.590
...but it was under my orders that
you assumed command of the ship.

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:44.900
Isn't that enough ?

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:46.680
Yes, sir.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:52.820
LTJG, I mean, Lieutenant, human beings are inconvenient things.

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:59.230
No one can be freed from one's class, status, position, and such things.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:07.240
We can only see others through the
filter of prejudices and preconceptions.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:11.030
I myself had also misjudged
you at the beginning.

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:15.980
As the brother of Countess Grünewald,
a 16-year-old Lieutenant Junior Grade...

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:19.620
...a model student and valedictorian of the military preparatory school.

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:22.030
Fortunately, even though
I'm an aristocrat...

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:24.260
...I'm just a baron who's from a
far from distinguished lineage...

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.430
...and I'm not completely immersed in aristocratic society.

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:31.400
I also joined the military late and I've seen the world outside it.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:36.810
Because of that, I think I know a few tricks to remove the "filter" of prejudices, just a little.

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.900
That's why you
left me in command.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.200
If I have to provide
a reason, then that{i.e. what he says above} is it.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.370
In any case, what are
you planning to do now ?

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.650
Aboard my ship, the position of
first officer is vacant at present, but...

00:20:51.830 --> 00:20:53.200
If possible, I'd like a transfer.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.240
That's in your best interests.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:01.730
It probably won't do any good to tell
you to look outside the military now...

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:06.320
...but you should at least experience many different departments within the military.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.370
I will write a recommendation letter for you.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.430
Thank you very much.

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:12.070
Then you may go.

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:12.820
Yes, sir.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:19.030
That same day, along with the promotion of Reinhard von Musel to Lieutenant...

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:22.180
...the special double-promotions 
of Lieutenant Haltram Beltram...

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:26.030
...and Seaman Rolf Zaidel, who died in the line of duty, were also announced.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:30.680
Four days later, after being transferred to office duties in the Military Ministry...

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:35.570
...Reinhard and Kircheis left the
Hameln II after their brief stint.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.000
Request permission to go ashore.

